AB  - The balance of computational complexity and detection accuracy in ultra-low-power embedded vision systems is crucial. In this paper, the reproducible implementation and evaluation of per-pixel frame differencing on the highly resourceconstrained XIAO ESP32 S3 camera module are provided. The experimental evaluation of the two modes of the per-pixel frame differencing approach, namely raw difference mode and summary mode, is carried out. The experimental evaluation is done in terms of the trade-off in throughput and latency and the memory usage of the approach. The experimental evaluation is carried out with varying illumination conditions. Although no new motion detection approach is proposed in this paper, the design pattern for the implementation of the approach in resource-constrained embedded vision systems is provided.  © 2026 IEEE.
