AB  - The rapid proliferation of Internet of Things (IoT) devices, coupled with the emergence of low-power wide-area networks (LPWANs), has created an urgent need for efficient, low-latency, and scalable data processing frameworks. This chapter explores the integration of Tiny Machine Learning (TinyML) and edge artificial intelligence (edge AI) as a promising solution to meet these demands. By enabling on-device intelligence, TinyML allows resource-constrained IoT nodes to perform localized data analytics, thereby reducing dependency on cloud infrastructure, lowering energy consumption, and enhancing data privacy. We present a comprehensive overview of the architectural considerations, key application domains, and performance trade-offs involved in deploying edge AI in LPWAN environments. In addition, we examine existing hardware and software platforms, discuss major deployment challenges, and highlight strategies for optimizing machine learning models under strict power, memory, and computational limitations. The chapter concludes by outlining future research directions aimed at achieving secure, scalable, and interpretable AI at the extreme edge. © 2026 selection and editorial matter, Khalid El Makkaoui, Ismail Lamaakal, Ibrahim Ouahbi, Yassine Maleh, and Ahmed A. Abd El-Latif; individual chapters, the contributors.
