AB  - With the intention of enabling low-power, resource-constrained devices like microcontrollers (MCUs) and edge devices to use the power of machine learning (ML), tiny machine learning, or TinyML, is a fast-growing field. This technology allows ML models to be deployed on devices with limited memory, processing capacity, and energy consumption, which makes it relevant for a range of applications where standard ML approaches are not practical. Real-time data processing, analysis, and action at the network edge have been revolutionized by TinyML, which has been driven into numerous fields by the merging of machine learning (ML) and the Internet of Things (IoT). There are many different use cases that TinyML can demonstrate. Examples of use cases include phenomenology, face detection, gesture recognition, keyword detection, sign language processing, ecological monitoring, image recognition, traffic control, environmental forecast, autonomous vehicle monitoring, cough detection, posture estimate, posture evaluation, respiratory symptoms, and always-on voice wake-up. Smart agriculture is one of TinyML’s most well-known application cases. Farmers can keep an eye on crop health, weather patterns, and soil conditions in real time by implementing TinyML models on sensor-equipped devices. These revelations pave the way for precision agriculture, in which data-driven choices maximize crop productivity, minimize resource consumption, and protect the environment. Another sector that TinyML has a big impact on is healthcare. Vital indications including blood oxygen levels, heart rate, and activity patterns can be continuously monitored by wearable devices that are embedded with TinyML models. Real-time anomaly detection capabilities enable these gadgets to notify patients or medical professionals about possible health problems. Furthermore, TinyML is transforming quality control and predictive maintenance in the field of industrial automation. Real-time decision-making at the edge is made possible by TinyML in autonomous systems, such as robots and drones. Ultimately, TinyML expands the application of machine learning into fields where traditional deployment barriers related to latency, power, and cost have made intelligent systems less viable. Its applications include consumer electronics, agriculture, healthcare, industrial automation etc. The potential of TinyML technology to revolutionize industries and enhance everyday life will only increase as it develops, adaptable, and sustainable solutions at the edge. © 2026 Scrivener Publishing LLC. All rights reserved.
