AB  - Battery State of Health (SoH) estimation is critical for autonomous systems, where mission decisions depend on reliable energy awareness. This work formulates SoH estimation as a bounded diagnostic service within a mission-aware architecture, combining controlled acquisition, measurement validation, and uncertainty-aware inference based on Gaussian Process Regression (GPR) fed with Electrochemical Impedance Spectroscopy (EIS) features. Moreover, predictive uncertainty is used to identify unreliable estimates and limit their propagation. Results show stable performance under nominal conditions and progressive degradation under increasing noise. An analysis of deployment feasibility on microcontroller (MCU) units indicates that the estimator can be implemented with limited memory and sub-millisecond latency. These results support the feasibility of on-device, uncertainty-aware battery diagnostics for resource-constrained autonomous systems.  © 2026 IEEE.
