AB  - The proceedings contain 50 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Microelectronics, Electromagnetics and Telecommunication. The topics include: An Effective Efficient Method for Object Detection and Classification Based on Deep Learning and CNN; an Innovative and Resilient Deep Learning Approach for a Weather Invariant Traffic Sign Identification System in a Dynamic Setting; machine Learning Classification Algorithms for Crop Prediction, Sensor Testing, and IoT-Based Soil Parameter Surveillance; an Automated Predetermined Method for Identifying Fenugreek Plant Diseases Using Color Sensors and IoT; A High-Speed Digital Approximation Multiplier Design and Performance Analysis for AI-VLSI Applications; Integrating Machine Learning Approaches to Detect Plant Diseases Through Crop Monitoring Using IOT Sensors and Live Image Captures; Analysis of the 7T-SRam Cell’s Development and Execution Employing a Body Bias Controller; secure-by-Design Wireless Frameworks for High-Reliability Cyber-Physical IoT Systems; scalable and Secure Remote Authentication for Resource-Constrained IoT-Based Smart Homes; robust Mutual Authentication for Distributed IoT Systems: Balancing Security and Efficiency; Leveraging IEC 61850 for Interoperable and Resilient Smart Grid Communication Architecture; AI-Enabled Log Analysis for Predictive Maintenance and Troubleshooting in Industrial IoT; towards Digital Forensics 4.0: A Multilevel Digital Forensics Framework for Internet of Things (IoT) Devices; ioT-Enabled Campus Energy Surveillance System with Raspberry Pi Pico Microcontroller; preface; performance Comparison Between Multilayer Perceptrons and Kolmogorov-Arnold Networks for Fault Detection in Automotive Engines; An AI-Powered Crop Disease Detection System for Potato Agriculture Using Ensemble Deep Learning; zero Trust Architecture: Redefining Security in the Digital World; AI-Driven Intrusion Detection Systems: Algorithms, Key Applications, Efficacy, Opportunities and Ethical Implications.
