TI  - Efficient training of deep neural networks on resource-constrained devices for industrial applications
PY  - 2025
T2  - Proceedings of SPIE - The International Society for Optical Engineering
VL  - 13803
C7  - 138032Q
DO  - 10.1117/12.3078229
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105022485962?origin=resultslist
AD  - Navoi State University of Mining and Technologies, Navoi, 210100, Uzbekistan
AD  - Bukhara State Technical University, Bukhara, Uzbekistan
AB  - Deep neural networks (DNNs) have shown remarkable success across many artificial intelligence applications, yet their computational and memory demands make them difficult to deploy on low-resource devices such as Raspberry Pi, microcontrollers, and mobile edge hardware. In real-time scenarios such as remote health monitoring, smart agriculture, and IoT-based automation create barriers to on-device AI implementation. This study focuses on optimizing DNNs for resource-constrained environments by employing Python-based techniques to compress and accelerate models without substantial accuracy loss. We propose a three-stage optimization approach combining pruning, quantization, and knowledge distillation. Model pruning reduces the number of unnecessary parameters, quantization converts model weights to low-precision formats (e.g., int8), and knowledge distillation transfers knowledge from a large teacher model to a smaller student model. These techniques are implemented using TensorFlow Lite and PyTorch Mobile frameworks. © 2025 SPIE.
