AB  - Alignment of large language models usually relies on gradient-based methods such as RLHF and DPO. However, when resources are limited, there are computational, memory and data efficiency bottlenecks for small language models (SLM). This paper proposes an evolution-based multi-agent logical alignment framework, Evo-Multi-SLM. The framework is evaluated on mathematical reasoning tasks, demonstrating that evolutionary strategies achieve gradient-free alignment with competitive efficiency. Experiments show that its multiple metrics significantly outperform the baseline and LoRA fine-tuning, establishing the potential of evolutionary strategies in the efficient resource alignment of SLMs. © 2026 IEEE.
