AB  - Multimodal sensor fusion on resource-constrained microcontrollers (MCUs) is critical for Internet of Things (IoT) applications requiring real-time edge intelligence. While attention mechanisms have revolutionized deep learning, their deployment on ultra-low-power devices with <256KB RAM remains prohibitive due to quadratic memory complexity. We propose TinyFusion-NAS, a hardware-aware neural architecture search framework that discovers lightweight attention-based architectures optimized for multimodal sensor fusion (IMU, audio, environmental sensors) on ARM Cortex-M4/M7 processors using the TinyML framework. Our search space includes linear attention variants, grouped query attention, adaptive sparsity patterns, and hybrid CNN-attention blocks co-optimized with INT8 quantization. Experiments on three embedded platforms (ESP32-S3, STM32H7, nRF52840) demonstrate that TinyFusion- NAS achieves 12.3% higher accuracy than MobileNetV3 while reducing memory by 3.2 × and latency by 2.8 ×, enabling real-time fusion at <2mW power. © 2026 IEEE.
