AB  - Person identification is the process of recognizing a person through his image, voice, gait, etc. A person is unique in different aspects like his look, his way of speech, walking style, etc. Person recognition is used in various systems for authentication, to provide security, for example in opening voice-based door lock, image-based bio-metric systems for attendance monitoring, police security systems for identifying criminals and tracking them. A person can be identified by listening to his voice. In this paper we propose a voice-based person identification system which uses Embedded machine learning. In this work we implemented a micro-controller-based machine learning framework which uses the persons voice to identify the person accurately. This has a wide variety of applications and advantages, which include low power requirements, low bandwidth, low latency, compact size of the system and all these leads to improved efficiency. Applications include voice-based authentication systems, voice-based door locks and voice-based access systems.  © 2026 COPYRIGHT SPIE.
