AB  - The proceedings contain 111 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Security and Cryptography. The topics include: Unveiling Hierarchical Machine Learning UDP–QUIC Intrusion Detection: Protocol-Aware Flow Analysis and a New Generated DDoS Dataset; CT-Monitor++: Improving the Certificate Transparency Ecosystem with Cryptographic and Security Checks; ringslip: Ring Signatures from the Lattice Isomorphism Problem; Scalable High-Throughput FPGA Architecture for SMAC Message Authentication Code; homeGuard: Community-Driven Hierarchical Federated Learning for Robust Smart-Home Intrusion Detection; a Framework for Context-Aware Read Authorization over Encrypted Data; finding Fake Base Stations with Directional Antenna Using Measurement Reports; Threat-Reactive Encryption: Real-Time ML-Driven Key Rotation for Adaptive Cryptographic Defense; slice & Dice: Privacy-Preserving Layered Attestation via Active Memory Introspection; PQKE–hCPABE: A Hybrid CP-ABE Scheme with Post-Quantum Key Exchange for Secure Multicast; a Capability-Driven Framework for Prioritizing Post-Quantum Cryptography Migration in Enterprise Architectures; A Maliciously Secure and Fully Decentralized Threshold FHE Scheme with Native RNS Acceleration; FLiPD: Privacy-Preserving Federated Learning via Multi-Party Computation and Differential Privacy; on Automating the Obfuscation of Malware Payloads: Zone, a bin2bin Metamorphic Engine; experimental Evaluation of Lightweight Encryption Algorithms on 16-bit Microcontrollers; A PQC-Enabled IoT Trust Architecture; third-Party Script Identification through Supervised Contrastive Learning on Behavioral Profiles; are Explanations Robust to Federated Poisoning? An Empirical Study in Cyber Threat Detection; a Game-Theoretic Approach for Optimal Multi-Target Defense Strategies in Programmable Networking; Compact and Low-Power ECC Processor Implementation over GF(2m ) for Resource-Constrained IoT Devices; A Bridged Sandbox–Honeypot Architecture for Behavi