AB  - This study presents ONB-En, a lightweight symmetric encryption algorithm designed for resource-constrained platforms such as IoT devices, embedded systems, and low-power microcontrollers. The algorithm was developed to address the growing need for fast, memory-efficient cryptographic solutions capable of protecting short-lived or low-risk data without the computational overhead of conventional encryption algorithms. ONB-En combines XOR-based key mixing, fixed byte permutation, and rotation operations to achieve low computational complexity while maintaining acceptable diffusion properties. The algorithm was evaluated using multiple real-world datasets ranging from 50 KB to 10 MB. Experimental results show that ONB-En encrypts data 3.3 times faster than AES, 2.1 times faster than Blowfish, and 5.4 times faster than RC4, with an average execution time of 0.41 ms per block. CPU utilization was reduced by 59% compared with AES, while memory requirements remained below 150 bytes of RAM and 1 KB of flash, outperforming the baseline algorithms. Security evaluation produced an avalanche score of 60.9%, an entropy value of 7.1 bits per byte, and a key sensitivity of 49.1%, demonstrating performance suitable for lightweight cryptographic applications. Although ONB-En is not intended to replace high-assurance encryption standards, it provides an efficient and predictable solution for resource-constrained environments where execution speed, minimal memory footprint, and implementation simplicity are prioritized over maximum cryptographic strength. These results demonstrate that ONB-En offers a practical balance between computational efficiency and security for real-time data protection in embedded, mobile, and other constrained computing environments. © The Author(s), under exclusive licence to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd. 2026.
