AB  - The proliferation of edge computing demands shifting intelligence from centralized clouds to resource-constrained devices. However, traditional edge nodes often rely on static, hard-coded logic that lacks the flexibility of modern service-based systems. This paper presents a demonstration of a lightweight, API- and event-driven software architecture designed to execute Complex Event Processing (CEP) in edge microcontroller-based systems. The proposed architecture decouples event ingestion, pattern evaluation, and action execution, enabling real-time event correlation and autonomous decision-making on low-resource devices such as microcontrollers. In addition, its embedded REST API management layer supports dynamic runtime reconfiguration of detection thresholds without firmware redeployment. By combining local CEP capabilities with MQTT-based inter-node communication, the system also enables collaborative event correlation and coordinated responses across multiple microcontroller-based edge nodes.  © 2026 IEEE.
