AB  - The deployment of artificial intelligence models on resource-constrained industrial edge devices requires systematic optimization of neural network architectures to meet strict latency, memory, and energy constraints. Traditional cloud-based inference approaches introduce unacceptable delays for real-time industrial control applications. This paper proposes a comprehensive Edge-AI inference pipeline that integrates neural network quantization, structured pruning, and hardware-aware compilation for multi-sensor industrial monitoring systems. The methodology is validated on real industrial telemetry data using embedded platforms (NVIDIA Jetson Nano, Raspberry Pi 4, and ARM Cortex-M microcontrollers). Experimental results demonstrate that the proposed pipeline achieves 4.2 × reduction in model size, 3.8 × inference speedup, and 2.1 × energy efficiency improvement while maintaining accuracy degradation below 1.2 % compared to baseline models. The optimized pipeline enables sub- 10 ms inference latency for real-time IIoT anomaly detection and predictive maintenance, while providing practical deployment guidelines and open-source implementation for practitioners.  © 2026 IEEE.
