AB  - Smart homes that rely on the cloud often have problems with high transmission latency, privacy risks, and a lot of extra bandwidth. This project proposes a decentralized edge-computing automation system that incorporates an Arduino Uno, an ESP8266 Wi-Fi module, a local Python edge gateway, and mobile rule engines like iOS Shortcuts to address these limitations. The local gateway takes care of heavy computational tasks, such as parsing complex JSON and logging data all the time. This lets the resource-constrained microcontroller work as a very optimized hardware abstraction layer. To get around strict hardware limits (2KB SRAM and 32KB Flash), advanced memory management techniques were used. The proposed system successfully achieved sub-second latency, eliminated hardware servo jitter, and enabled highly customizable, local automation routines without reliance on proprietary cloud ecosystems, proving the viability of decentralized, low-cost IoT computing. Copyright © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
