AD  - Madanapalle Institute of Technology & Science (MITS), Deemed to be University, Dept. of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Madanapalle, India
AB  - This research presents the design and verification of a lightweight CNN accelerator based on a cross-layer architecture that tightly couples algorithmic modeling with hardware implementation. The rapid growth of IoT has driven the adoption of TinyML, where deploying reliable CNNs on resource-constrained microcontrollers and low-cost FPGAs remains challenging due to strict memory, latency, and power constraints. The proposed workflow integrates MATLAB-based quantization-aware architectural design, Register-Transfer Level (RTL) verification on a Xilinx Artix-7 FPGA, and system-level power profiling on an STM32F407 microcontroller using virtual prototyping. Experimental results demonstrate that the proposed INT8 quantized architecture achieves a footprint accuracy of 98.24% accuracy with only 0.48% degradation compared to the FP32 baseline while significantly reducing computational and memory overheads. Furthermore, Hardware-in-the-Loop verification confirms the functional correctness of the system and validates that Dynamic Voltage and Frequency Scaling (DVFS) effectively reduces power consumption during idle operating states. These results highlight the suitability of the proposed accelerator for energy-efficient TinyML applications at the edge.  © 2026 IEEE.
