AB  - As of March 2021, TinyJAMBU is one of the 12 finalists in the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) competition launched to standardize lightweight cryptographic algorithms, suitable for resource-constrain devices (e.g. RFID sensors, microcontrollers, embedded devices, industrial controllers). This paper reports on the software implementation details of TinyJAMBU on a Siemens S7–1200 Programmable Logic Controller. We evaluate the execution speed and memory requirements of each variant of the algorithm on this industrial controller. © 2023, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG.
