TI  - StegSecure-IoT: Enhancing Personal IoT Data Privacy via Compression-Based Crypto-Steganography
PY  - 2025
T2  - 2025 5th Asian Conference on Innovation in Technology, ASIANCON 2025
DO  - 10.1109/ASIANCON66527.2025.11280607
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105031359756?origin=resultslist
AD  - Coep Technological University, Electronics and Telecommunication Department, Pune, India
AB  - The Internet of Things (IoT) ecosystem comprises interconnected microcontroller-based sensors that continuously collect and exchange personal data in real-time. However, the lightweight nature of embedded devices makes them particularly vulnerable to data breaches and cyber threats, especially when traditional encryption algorithms exceed their processing capabilities. To address this, we propose a double-layered security mechanism for personal IoT sensor data using a compression-driven Crypto-Steganography approach. Our method integrates AES-128 encryption with Zstandard compression to provide strong confidentiality and enhanced transmission efficiency. A novel Color-Channel Substitution strategy is employed, guided by statistical analysis of both cover images and sensor data, to maximize embedding capacity and robustness. Unlike conventional steganography that uses recognizable images, our system utilizes randomly generated images as cover media, further obscuring potential data leakage vectors. Experimental evaluations demonstrate a 30% improvement in embedding capacity and increased resistance to steganalysis, verified through chi-square, histogram, entropy analysis, and SSIM metrics. As a proof of concept, personal location data is acquired from a GPS module,heartbeat sensor interfaced with a Raspberry Pi, then processed using our Crypto-Steganography method before being securely transmitted over WiFi and stored in a cloud database. This approach offers an efficient and secure solution for protecting sensitive personal sensor data in resource-constrained IoT environments.  © 2025 IEEE.
