AD  - Azerbaijan Technical University, Faculty of Information and Telecommunication Technologies, Baku, Azerbaijan
AB  - Modern embedded systems are evolving quickly, demanding innovative approaches to software development across various domains. Selecting the right programming language is crucial for balancing efficient resource utilization with faster development cycles in microcontroller applications. The objective of this research is to analyze the suitability of C, Rust, Python, and Lua for developing microcontroller-based systems. An assessment of each language's suitability involves examining factors such as memory footprint, execution speed, memory safety, and development complexity within resource-constrained environments. Practical validation is conducted on the ESP8266 microcontroller, selected for its affordability and native support for all four languages, providing a solid foundation for comparative analysis. By exploring the strengths and weaknesses of each language in the context of microcontroller programming, this work aims to provide developers with a framework for making informed language choices, optimizing both performance and development speed based on specific application requirements. © 2025 IEEE.
