TI  - IoT Based Home Appliances: A Revolutionary Approach for 21st Century Smart Homes in South Asian Urban Cities
PY  - 2025
T2  - 2025 2nd International Conference on Advanced Computing and Emerging Technologies, ACET 2025
DO  - 10.1109/ACET67282.2025.11430352
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105037898331?origin=resultslist
AD  - Abes Engineering College, U.P., Ghaziabad, India
AB  - Internet of Things (IoT) revolutionized home automation to achieve intelligent, secure, and energy-saving living. Sensors (DHT11 temperature-humidity sensor, MQ-2 for gas sensors), ESP8266 microcontroller, and the Blynk mobile app are used to make remote real-time monitoring and automation possible. Threshold-based and event-based algorithms are used to provide smart, context-aware decisions, such as fans or exhaust system switches based on environmental factors, in order to improve comfort and security. The system supports energy consumption monitoring, gas leak sensing, predictive maintenance alerts, and personalized automation sequences. Being open source and low cost, the system is scalable and adaptable, making it easily upgradable or deployable in massive numbers on a citywide scale to cover individual households. The users can easily control and monitor appliances, optimizing their energy use and extending device lifespan. Experimental trials are about 98-99% accurate in appliance control and instant sensor-initiated responses. The primary contributions are the fusion of sensor-based automation with cloud communication, a smart-home proof-of-concept that scales, and real-time energy optimization and safety monitoring smart algorithms. This research offers real-world proof-of-concept for IoT-based smart homes in resource-constrained urban environments.  © 2025 IEEE.
