AB  - The research outlined in this paper focuses on designing and implementing a secure data transmission system within a smart home environment, utilizing the RC4-streamcipher (RSC) algorithm. The emphasis lies on integrating robust encryption mechanisms into sensor data, allowing for secure data aggregation directly at the edge through an IoT-enabled hardware setup. Within this system, sensor data undergoes encryption using the RSC algorithm within Arduino-Uno microcontrollers (AUM), ensuring the real-time protection of crucial metrics such as voltage, current, power, energy, frequency, and power factor. While the use of RSC presents certain challenges, particularly in the generation of secret keys, future investigations could explore dynamic key generation techniques to bolster the algorithm's resilience against potential cryptographic attacks. The findings of this study showcase the practicality and efficacy of the proposed methodology, shedding light on secure edge computing in smart home environments. By addressing security concerns related to data transmission and processing, this research contributes valuable insights to the field. © 2024 IEEE.
