AB  - This paper presents a non-intrusive, cost-effective HAR system that utilizes Wi-Fi Channel State Information (CSI) collected from the ESP32 microcontroller [2], [3]. By analysing signal distortions caused by human motion, the system classifies activities such as walking, running, and standing without the need for cameras or wearables [1], [4]. Deep learning modelsincluding Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN), Long ShortTerm Memory (LSTM), and a hybrid CNN+LSTM-were trained using synthetically generated CSI datasets [5], [6]. Among them, the CNN+LSTM hybrid model achieved the highest classification accuracy of 77.0% with improved F1-score and generalization capability [8], [9]. This work demonstrates the feasibility of using Wi-Fi CSI for passive human activity recognition and highlights its potential in privacy-sensitive and resource-constrained applications [3], [6]. © 2025 IEEE.
