AB  - PPG-enabled wearables are increasingly prevalent and have the potential to improve remote healthcare systems significantly. However, their implementation can be challenging under resource constraints. To alleviate these constraints, this article proposed a lightweight autoencoder-based lossy PPG compression system for data streaming applications. The system reduces the amount of transmitted data by a factor of 8 while maintaining the information with the signal RMSE at 0.026 and peak MAE at 0.020. This is possible through the loss-conditional training approach on specific task learning. Its practical functionality and advantages are verified on a resource-constrained Docker container and an Arduino Nano 33 BLE microcontroller board. This system cut down transmission energy consumption by 84%. © 2023 IEEE.
