TI  - TINYLOCK A Lightweight and Adaptable Encryption Algorithm for Enhancing IoT Security on ATtiny85 Microcontrollers
PY  - 2025
T2  - Proceedings of the National Conference on Communications, NCC
IS  - 2025
DO  - 10.1109/NCC63735.2025.10983402
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105010683223?origin=resultslist
AD  - RGUKT AP IIIT Nuzvid, Department of ECE, Nuzvid, India
AB  - TINY-LOCK, a lightweight encryption algorithm tailored for resource-constrained microcontrollers like the ATtiny85, widely used in IoT applications. Leveraging a compact Feistel network with a custom 4-bit S-Box, It achieves secure encryption with minimal computational overhead. Our results show that it encrypts a 32-bit block in just 1,500 clock cycles, outperforming popular ciphers like TEA and Speck, which require up to 3,000 cycles. It uses only 800 bytes of flash and 64 bytes of RAM, making it ideal for low-power devices. Performance benchmarks across I2C, SPI, and UART protocols reveal a 35% reduction in latency and 25% decrease in power consumption compared to existing algorithms. It demonstrates strong resilience against differential attacks with probabilities below 2-30, ensuring robust security. This makes TINY-LOCK a powerful, efficient, and secure solution for next-generation IoT devices. © 2025 IEEE.
