AB  - Recently, how to attain high reliability and multimodal identity authentication on resource-constrained embedded platforms is now an important technical problem. This paper proposes a multimodal lock authentication system which adopts fingerprint, NFC, and PIN integration into one system based on STM32F407VET6 microcontroller and utilizes a complex model with hierarchical fusion and real-time scheduler (HFDAS). The model innovates on previous serial and parallel fusion models by developing a three layer structure. The first layer, estimates modality confidence by dynamically allocating weight among the three modalities. The second layer, the last finite state machine, provides priority switching among modalities based on context. The third layer, utilizes an interrupt-driven task scheduler using FreeRTOS, providing real-time fusion and arbitration among multimodal inputs. Experimental results show the proposed system maintains response latency under 200 ms, with an accompanying False Accept Rate (FAR) of less than 0.15%. © 2025 IEEE.
