AD  - STMicroelectronics, Ipa Division, Catania, Italy
AB  - Deploying deep neural networks on embedded systems is challenging due to stringent constraints on memory, compute, and power. DISTILLO (aDvanced Interactive ST knowledge distILLation) is a knowledge distillation framework tailored for classification tasks in resource-limited environments. It features two strategies: DISTILLO-Classical, using dynamic loss weighting with Kullback-Leibler or Jensen-Shannon divergence, and DISTILLO-Ensemble, which combines multiple student models distilled at different temperatures. Jensen-Shannon divergence is adopted to provide symmetric, bounded, and stable gradients, improving the robustness of the training. Experiments using Vision Transformers as teachers and lightweight CNNs as students show that DISTILLO-Classical achieves up to +5.37% accuracy gain on CIFAR-100 and +4.42% on Imagenette. DISTILLO-Ensemble further improves performance, reaching +13.97% and +8.32% gains, respectively, with minimal memory and latency overhead. DISTILLO enables the effective deployment of deep models on embedded platforms such as STM32 microcontrollers. © 2025 IEEE.
