AD  - Instituto De Investigación E Innovación En Electrónica, Universidad Don Bosco, Soyapango, El Salvador
AB  - This paper introduces CLOG, a cube-based lightweight key-mutation scheme designed for resourceconstrained IoT devices. CLOG represents a 96-bit state as six 16bit faces and applies a sequence of table-driven surface rotations, followed by a simple parameter mutation, to produce a new key and mutated control parameter. The design achieves constanttime execution, minimal memory usage, and predictable latency, making it suitable for microcontrollers such as the ESP8266. Experimental results confirm that CLOG can provide efficient and deterministic credential mutation, complementing standard cryptographic primitives in constrained environments.  © 2025 IEEE.
