AD  - School of Cyber Engineering, Xidian University, Xi'an, China
AB  - Federated Learning (FL) on resource-constrained Microcontroller Units (MCUs)-the cornerstone of the IoT-is considered largely infeasible due to prohibitive on-device training costs. This paper introduces μ-Fed, a full-stack co-designed system that makes robust FL on low-cost MCUs a reality for multimodal cardiovascular monitoring. The core of μ-Fed is a novel memory-efficient training algorithm that reduces peak RAM usage by over 70%, making on-device backpropagation feasible on commodity hardware. This core innovation is integrated with a hardware-aware data pipeline for high-precision sensing and a robustness-aware aggregation protocol that adapts to real-world data quality using Signal Quality Indices (SQI). Evaluation on a physical testbed of 30 STM32-based nodes demonstrates that μ-Fed achieves up to 15% faster convergence on Non-IID data distributions. This work provides the first complete, validated blueprint for deploying practical FL at the extreme edge. © 2025 IEEE.
