AB  - This paper addresses the problem of efficient data transmission from wearable biomedical sensors via wireless communication channels in human motion biomechanics monitoring systems. A combined approach to sensor data compression is proposed, which includes preliminary octahedral transformation of accelerometer vectors followed by the use of the lossless Sprintz compression algorithm. This method accounts for the vector nature of the signal, reduces redundancy, and improves compression efficiency without significantly increasing the computational or memory load. Experimental evaluation demonstrated that the application of octahedral encoding reduces accelerometer data volume to 57% (compared to 84% without transformation), and the total transmitted data volume - to 61%, depending on the type of activity. The proposed approach is suitable for implementation on resource-constrained microcontroller-based platforms and is recommended for use in real-time systems. © 2025 IEEE.
