TI  - Efficient Deep Learning: Model Optimization Strategies for Resource-Constrained Devices
PY  - 2025
T2  - 2025 4th International Conference on Embedded Systems and Artificial Intelligence, ESAI 2025
DO  - 10.1109/ESAI67033.2025.11438600
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105035998580?origin=resultslist
AD  - Sidi Mohamed Ben Abdellah University, LIASSE Laboratory, Fez, Morocco
AB  - TinyML brings machine learning inference to microcontrollers that operate under tight memory, compute, and energy constraints. This paper explores model optimization for such devices with a focus on quantization. We compare posttraining quantization and quantization-aware training on a compact convolutional neural network for the MNIST dataset. Our quantization-aware training recipe combines Parameterized Clipping Activation for activations with Learned Step Size Quantization for weights. In our experiments, Our QAT model uses 4-bit weights on the second convolution (Conv2), keeps Conv1 and the final fully-connected (FC) layer at 8-bit, and applies 8-bit PACT-clipped activations throughout. This approach preserved accuracy close to the floating-point baseline. At the same time, the weights-only storage dropped from about 196.8 KB to roughly 40 KB, about 5× smaller than FP32. We report accuracy, model size, and practical deployment notes relevant to embedded back ends. © 2025 IEEE.
