AD  - American University of Beirut, Environment and Sustainable Development Unit (ESDU), Faculty of Agricultural and Food Sciences, Beirut, Lebanon
AB  - This study investigates the integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Internet of Things (IoT) technologies for energy management in the Urban Oasis Smart Hub, developed by the Environment and Sustainable Development Unit (ESDU) at the American University of Beirut (AUB), Lebanon. The research addresses the critical energy inefficiencies in Lebanon, where technical losses in the national grid and reliance on private generators strain the economy and worsen environmental challenges. The implemented AI-based energy management solution achieved daily energy savings of 12.47 kWh and reduced carbon emissions by 24.25 kg per day. To do that, an AI-driven occupancy detection model, with a precision of 87.5%, was deployed to minimize unnecessary energy consumption. The system also integrated renewable energy sources to enhance sustainability and stability further. The system's financial performance showed an annual return on investment (ROI) of 11.41%, demonstrating the economic feasibility of AI-driven energy solutions in resource-constrained environments. The findings underscore the adaptability of AI and IoT technologies to local energy challenges in Lebanon and highlight their potential for addressing energy crises in similar regions. © 2025 IEEE.
