AB  - This paper presents the design and simulation of a low-power encryption module for secure data transmission in sensor-driven systems. The proposed lightweight encryption engine is described in VHDL, interfaced with a microcontroller through the SPI protocol, and synthesized using Xilinx Vivado with constraints targeting a Spartan-7 FPGA. The encryption scheme employs XOR-based logic with LFSR-driven key evolution and optional bit-position scrambling. Security, performance, and estimated power metrics, derived from Vivado synthesis and implementation reports, are discussed in relation to AES, DES, and RSA. Results indicate that the proposed design is suitable for energy-constrained embedded applications.  © 2025 IEEE.
