AB  - Cloudlets are a new technology in IoT, and the architecture and networking of cloudlets is an emerging area of research. The basic building block of cloudlets are SoCs or powerful microcontrollers; whether it is a SoC or a microcontroller, both are severely resource-constrained. In this paper, we are looking at the design of cloudlets using Qualcomm Snapdragon 410c. Though 410c is more powerful when compared to microcontroller-based systems, it is still constrained in terms of processing power and memory. End devices requests task to be executed on the cloudlet. Multiple requests from multiple end devices may be received by the cloudlets system at a given point in time. A cloudlet system is a distributed computing system which cannot run the existing uniprocessing or multiprocessing task scheduling algorithms. In this paper, we propose a new algorithm for distributed task scheduling with load balancing on cloudlets. © 2023, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd.
