AB  - Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems face persistent challenges in multi-turn conversational settings, particularly in tracking evolving contexts while maintaining computational efficiency. This paper introduces an enhanced Dynamic Context Tuning (DCT) framework that addresses these challenges through three key innovations: (1) hierarchical memory management with multi-tiered context organization, enabling O(log n) retrieval complexity; (2) rank-adaptive LoRA techniques for dynamic parameter allocation across model layers; and (3) semantic-preserving context compression that achieves a 71% token reduction while maintaining a BERTScore above 0.91. The improved DCT framework achieves 89.3 % Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) accuracy-a 6.6 percentage point gain over the baseline-while reducing inference latency by 42% and memory usage by 50%. Comprehensive evaluation across calendar management, healthcare planning, and home automation domains reveals statistically significant gains (p<0.001) with large effect sizes (Cohen's d>2.0). These results demonstrate that targeted architectural optimizations can yield substantial improvements over frontier models while remaining suitable for deployment in resource-constrained environments. © 2025 IEEE.
