AB  - This paper presents a systematic evaluation of quantization strategies for deploying lightweight convolutional neural networks (CNNs) on resource-constrained microcontrollers. The study investigates three deployment approaches - full-precision floating-point (FP32), static INT8 quantization with per-tensor granularity, and static INT8 quantization with per-channel granularity - implemented using TensorFlow Lite for Microcontrollers. A custom CNN model was deployed on two hardware platforms: a conventional dual-core microcontroller and an advanced variant equipped with dedicated INT8 AI acceleration hardware. Inference performance was assessed in terms of memory usage, execution latency, and classification consistency across quantization schemes and architectures. The results provide practical insights into how quantization configuration and hardware choice affect the efficiency of neural network inference in embedded environments. This work highlights the importance of model-hardware co-optimization to enable scalable and reliable edge AI applications. © 2025 IEEE.
